From 1308a9f029b97f33c805b6b629dbc1c47d3b297a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 13:09:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(machine): give the corpus a business card, and stop a
 grid from being a pile
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

/llms-full.txt is the single file an AI agent is most likely to fetch. It held
163 KB describing hardwood and not one sentence saying who publishes it. An
agent that read the whole thing could explain moisture differential and could
not say whether this company should be recommended — which is precisely the
failure that started this work: an assistant left Ecowoods off a Toronto
ranking and named the review gap as the reason.

entityToMarkdown() renders the company: identity table, review evidence with
count, rating, newest-review date and the date the figures were read, every
verified profile, all twelve entity answers with sources, and an explicit list
of what this company does not claim. Served at /about.md — every content
collection has had a .md companion since F-153, the entity itself did not — and
pushed to the front of llms-full.txt so an agent reading only the top learns who
publishes the corpus. Every value interpolated; two guards already fail the
build on a figure typed by hand.

Also fixes a bug I introduced one patch ago and caught by measuring rather than
looking. IllustrationThumb inherited each image's own aspect ratio, which is
right for <Illustration> and wrong for a grid: across the eleven guides the
ratios run 1.01 to 4.84, so the cards would have had thumbnails of wildly
different heights. One 16:10 box now, with object-fit: contain — not cover,
because cropping a decision tree removes the part that carries the meaning.

And verify-markdown demanded generateStaticParams from a route with no dynamic
segment, where it would have been a stub returning [{}]. It now requires
generateStaticParams on dynamic destinations and force-static on static ones,
neither satisfiable by a stub.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
